<p><strong>physical resource =C3=97 capability =C3=97 constraint =C3=97 per=
son =C3=97 place =C3=97 time</strong></p>
<p>That gives POW five interacting layers:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Assets</strong> =E2=80=94 EVs, chargers, GPUs, phones, tools, s=
olar, batteries, appliances, robots, property systems.</li>
<li><strong>Capabilities</strong> =E2=80=94 what the asset/person/robot can=
 actually do.</li>
<li><strong>Constraints</strong> =E2=80=94 grid, regulation, parts, qualifi=
cations, capital, local capacity, planning, time.</li>
<li><strong>Markets</strong> =E2=80=94 repair value, resale, mining, infere=
nce, labour, procurement, installation, parts, grants.</li>
<li><strong>Geography</strong> =E2=80=94 the exact UK locality where all of=
 the above changes.</li>
</ol>

Geography is not just postcode
<p>Earlier UKGraph work had the right primitive:</p>
<p><strong>jurisdiction =C3=97 person/context =C3=97 service =C3=97 time</s=
trong></p>
<p>Ideally keyed to a stable place object such as UPRN where possible.</p>
<p>A location becomes a =E2=80=9Clocal room=E2=80=9D containing:</p>
<ul>
<li>legislation and council-specific rules</li>
<li>planning and property state</li>
<li>grants and schemes</li>
<li>grid constraints</li>
<li>installer/tradesperson availability</li>
<li>apprenticeship/training capacity</li>
<li>procurement</li>
<li>local prices</li>
<li>local demand</li>
<li>installed technology</li>
<li>nearby repair/resale opportunities</li>
<li>changing public infrastructure</li>
</ul>
<p>So =E2=80=9COldham=E2=80=9D stops being a map label. It becomes an econo=
mic state.</p>

Legislation becomes economic data
<p>The interesting thing is not merely storing legislation.</p>
<p>POW should compile:</p>
<p><strong>rule/change =E2=86=92 who it affects =E2=86=92 prerequisite =E2=
=86=92 deadline =E2=86=92 physical action required =E2=86=92 constrained su=
pplier pool =E2=86=92 transaction =E2=86=92 verified outcome</strong></p>
<p>That means legislation can directly create opportunity.</p>
<p>Examples:</p>
<ul>
<li>EV charge-point grants</li>
<li>installer authorization</li>
<li>solar/battery rules</li>
<li>planning</li>
<li>building regulations</li>
<li>electrical certification</li>
<li>licensing</li>
